 "statement": {
  "status": "present",
  "value": "ChatApp() has one shared channel. addBot(botName, botType) adds a bot and returns true, or returns false when the type is unknown or a bot with that name already exists. sendMessage(userId, text) logs the user message and the bot replies. getRecentMessages(k) returns the last min(k, log size) log entries, oldest first. Bot types (inferred, since the preview cuts them off): \"echo\" answers a message starting with \"/echo \" with the rest of the text; \"reverse\" answers a message starting with \"/reverse \" with the rest reversed; \"count\" answers the exact message \"/count\" with the number of user messages in the channel so far, including this one, in decimal. Log entries are \"<sender>: <text>\". After a user message is logged, bots react in the order they were added; bot replies are logged but never trigger bots.  Every method call is answered in call order on one instance; void methods return nothing.",
  "provenance": [
   {
    "repository": "gamma",
    "revision": null,
    "path": "projects/algorithm_solver/catalogue/authored/hack2hire-chunk10-a-20261028-v1/contracts.json",
